                <pb facs="0949" n="843" xml:id="pg843"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Brown to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-07-16"><hi rendition="#italic">July 16,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Brown reports that he was told by President Estrada that he had received, at
                    9 o’clock a.m., a telegram from President Diaz, indicating dawn of to-day for
                    commencement of armistice, which is obviously impossible as well as most
                    embarrassing to Guatemala. He adds that President Estrada is ready for immediate
                    armistice, but at feasible hour mutually agreed upon, and that Minister Merry
                    will be notified as soon as President Estrada indicates hour for armistice to
                    commence. Mr. Brown reports that he has been informed by the President of
                    Guatemala that more Salvador troops entered to-day,)</p>
            </div>
